# Guided recovery

Use the live media or recovery environment to run:
```bash
sudo workstation-recover
```

It unlocks LUKS, mounts @root, @home, @snapshots, and /boot (ESP), bind-mounts proc/sys/dev/run,
and chroots. Type exit to unmount and close LUKS.

For signed recovery entries, use systemd-boot to select a protected snapshot UKI.
